main.py
--unwind 3

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
differential2 §12b residual: cross-branch UnboundLocalError. PLR:
f(False) raises UnboundLocalError because x is assigned only on the
True branch. The straight-line detection misses it (x's local symbol
exists from the if-branch conversion), so CBMC reports SUCCESSFUL. The
KNOWNBUG regex states the PLR-correct VERIFICATION FAILED. A sound
path-sensitive fix needs a runtime is-bound flag set at every binding
site; a single-chokepoint flag caused false positives, so this stays a
documented residual (sound miss, not a false alarm).
